## Lore

A Powerlord is a Kydian warrior rebuilt with bio-wizard implants, mechanisms and devices into something far stronger than an ordinary Overlord. The process strains the body so badly that it cuts a Kydian''s life to about 90 years, but living that long still seems a fine thing to a Kydian, and being chosen is a great honor. About a third of the Splugorth''s Kydian troops are Powerlords.

## Appearance

A Powerlord looks just like an Overlord, down to the Overlord power armor, 8 to 10 feet tall and 400 to 600 lbs. The differences are the bio-wizard staffs it carries, possible augmentations such as extra limbs or a third eye, and an even more muscular build.

## Renegades

Powerlords are as fanatically loyal as Overlords, and one who is not is seen as an ingrate or a psychotic. Rogues are unwelcome in Atlantis and are attacked, captured or killed by Splugorth minions. Those who act against the Splugorth are hunted down and killed, usually by one or two Conservators.

## Equipment

Powerlords use almost anything but favor Splugorth bio-technology, and otherwise love high-powered variable lasers, particle beam rifles and rail guns. Standard issue: the Staff of Power, Overlord power armor, a psi-interrogator, two purirobes, two clotrobes, 1D4 magic leeches, 1D4 zombitrons, and two further kinds of bio-wizard device, weapon or microbe (two doses). Only high ranking officers receive a rune weapon, never a greatest one.

## GM Notes

The book calls the Powerlord a rarity as a player character, to start at first or second level. NPC Powerlords average level 1D4+2.
